    control_path: ControlPathRuleValue | None = Field(None, description="“Home Assistant access”: hub = no Home Assistant key (with remote access a read-only one), reading and switching only through the hub; checked = the device's HA user only reads, switching goes through the checked integration action; direct = full HA rights, rules only in the app.")
    access_hours: AccessHours | None = Field(None, description='“Access hours”: the device has access only inside the windows (hub time zone); outside it stays paired and sees nothing. With the access switch in Home Assistant: access = schedule (when enabled) AND switch on.')
    setup_devices: ProfileRuleValuesSetupDevices | None = Field(None, description='“Set up new devices”: enabled = this device may set up new devices by QR code or code (onboard_confirm) and invite guests (guest_invite_create, needs kind guest); kinds = the profile kinds it may give ($defs/profile_kind: guest, child, panel, tv, house_sitter, babysitter, person; unique, so never more than there are kinds). Never more rights than its own (onboarding checks every offered profile). Applies only to profiles of kind person; boundaries guest and parental controls: off.')
    family_manager: StrictBool | None = Field(None, description='Family manager: may manage the kids rules of the children in family_children (device property) within what the profile does not fix, answer their requests and see their activity.')
    babysitter_requests: StrictBool | None = Field(None, description="“Answer children's requests”: a babysitter device receives the children's requests (“Can I have more time?”) while it has access and is at home, and may answer Yes 15/30 min, Yes until the end of babysitting or No. No rule changes, no blocked devices, no activity. Only profiles of kind babysitter.")
    access_requests: StrictBool | None = Field(None, description='“Ask for early access”: outside its access hours the device may ask for access now; the devices that set it up or may set up its kind (babysitter: also the family managers) answer Yes with a duration or No. Takes effect only with access hours (rule access_hours enabled).')
    app_settings: ProfileRuleValuesAppSettingsValue | None = Field(None, description="Settings in the app: hidden, only with the device's remote PIN, open.")
    app_settings_biometrics: StrictBool | None = Field(None, description='Face ID / Touch ID may replace the remote PIN (app_settings = pin).')
    remote_control: ProfileRuleValuesRemoteControl | None = Field(None, description='When away: level per device type and per entity while the device is connected over the external route (Nabu Casa or the HA external URL); at home it has no effect. Precedence entity > domain:device_class > domain > default. control = operate; view = show only (exception: the safe direction of data/quick-access.json safe_direction - lock a lock, arm an alarm); hidden = not shown at all. Applies in the app, widgets/controls, Siri and on the watch; combined with quick access and kids rules the strictest value wins (docs/profiles.md). Keys of domains: a Home Assistant domain or domain:device_class (like kids_rule_type).')
    areas: ProfileRuleValuesAreas | None = Field(None, description="Visible areas. all = every active area; selected = the listed areas, areas with one of the tags and (own_area) the device's own area; nothing selected = no area (fail closed). In resolved values (client_config) the hub has replaced own_area by the concrete id: own_area is always false there.")
